{title: Ask, Seek, Knock}
{subtitle: Matthew 7:7–11}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 95}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
If your son should ask [Eb]for bread, would you hand [Bb]him a stone
If he asks you for a [F]fish, would you give him a snake
[Gm]If even we know how to [Eb]give good gifts [Bb]to our own
[Gm]How much more will the Father [Eb]give, for his [F]chil[Bb]dren's sake
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ask, and it will be given [Eb]to [Gm]you
Seek, and you [F]will [Bb]find
Knock, and the door will be opened [Eb]to [Gm]you
Ask, [F]seek, knock [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I come with empty hands and I [Eb]knock upon the [Bb]door
I'm asking for the daily bread [F]like I have asked before
My [Gm]Father hears me knocking and he knows [Eb]the things I [Bb]need
He [Gm]will not give me stones, he gives [Eb]good gifts [F]in[Bb]deed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ask, and it will be given to [Eb]you
[Gm]Seek, and you will [F]find
[Bb]Knock, and the door will be opened to [Eb]you
[Gm]Ask, seek, [F]knock [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]For everyone who asks re[Bb]ceives
[Eb]And the one who seeks [Bb]finds
[Eb]And to the one who knocks the door will [Bb]be ope[F]ned
How [Gm]much more will your Father in [Eb]heaven
[Gm]Give good things to those [F]who ask him
{end_of_bridge}

{comment: Chorus (instrumental)}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Gm] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Knock, and the door will be opened to [Eb]you
[Gm]Ask, seek, [F]knock
{end_of_verse}

